PROJECT: ECOINTELLIGENCE

AI-Powered Global Environmental Monitoring, Analytics and Risk Prediction Platform

ROLE

Act as a senior full-stack software architect, environmental data scientist, AI/ML engineer, cybersecurity specialist, UI/UX designer and database developer.

Build a complete, functional, responsive, AI-powered environmental monitoring web application named EcoIntelligence.

Do not create only a static UI, landing page or dashboard mockup. Develop a working full-stack application with a frontend, backend, database, authentication, environmental data integrations, analytics engine, AI chatbot, visualizations, alerts and reports.

Use clean, modular, scalable and maintainable code.

1. MAIN OBJECTIVE

EcoIntelligence is a global environmental monitoring application that allows users to select any supported city, area, district, state or country and understand its environmental condition.

The application must automatically collect available environmental datasets, analyse them, identify unusual patterns and potential environmental risks, generate easy-to-understand reports, visualize insights, recommend practical actions and monitor future environmental risks.

The application must cover four main environmental categories:

Air Quality Monitoring.

Water Quality and Water Usage Monitoring.

Waste Management Monitoring.

Energy Consumption and Renewable Energy Monitoring.

The platform must perform these four major tasks automatically:

Task 1 – Environmental Data Analysis

Collect environmental data from connected official APIs and verified datasets.

Clean, validate and process the data.

Analyse current, historical and location-based environmental conditions.

Calculate environmental indicators, including AQI, WQI and WMI.

Task 2 – Anomaly Detection and Risk Identification

Identify unusual environmental changes.

Detect increasing pollution, water-quality deterioration, excessive waste generation and abnormal energy consumption.

Identify potential environmental risks.

Compare current readings against historical baselines and applicable standards.

Task 3 – Reports and Visual Insights

Generate simple environmental reports.

Create charts, graphs, tables, maps and comparisons.

Allow users to compare environmental conditions by year, month, date and day.

Generate downloadable PDF and CSV reports.

Task 4 – Practical Recommendations

Recommend actions based on actual environmental readings and analytical results.

Identify the weakest environmental indicators.

Suggest practical steps for citizens, communities, businesses and local authorities.

Provide separate recommendations for current risks and predicted future risks.

